  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_01. Let quadrilateral ABCD be a 4-sided figure with AB = 8, BC = 6, CD = 10, DA = 12. Let quadrilateral MNPQ be a 4-sided figure with NP = 3, PQ = 5. ABCD is dilated to form MNPQ with scale factor 0.5, centered at point P_center. Find the length of MN in MNPQ.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A video game designer is creating a scaled-down version of an original controller design. The original controller ABCD has four buttons arranged in a quadrilateral pattern with distances AB = 8 cm, BC = 6 cm, CD = 10 cm, and DA = 12 cm between them.\n\nTo fit on a smaller handheld device, the designer shrinks the controller using a dilation with scale factor 0.5, centered at point P_center. This creates the new controller layout MNPQ.\n\nThe designer has already measured two of the button distances on the new controller: NP = 3 cm and PQ = 5 cm. However, she needs to know the distance MN on the scaled-down controller to ensure the buttons are properly spaced for the handheld device.\n\nWhat should the length of MN be on the new controller?"
